.TH LIBMPQ__ARCHIVE_CREATE_MPQE_IO 3 2026-11-18 "The MoPaQ archive library"
.SH NAME
libmpq__archive_create_mpqe_io \- create MPQE transport in caller-owned storage
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
.B #include <libmpq/mpq.h>
.sp
.BI "int32_t libmpq__archive_create_mpqe_io("
.BI "        mpq_archive_s **" "archive,"
.BI "        void *" "context,"
.BI "        libmpq_read_at_fn " "read_at,"
.BI "        libmpq_write_at_fn " "write_at,"
.BI "        libmpq_flush_fn " "flush,"
.BI "        const uint8_t *" "code,"
.BI "        size_t " "code_size,"
.BI "        const mpq_archive_create_options_s *" "options"
.BI ");"
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
Create a fresh MPQ archive and write its MPQE transport into an initially
empty caller-owned sink at logical offset zero. NULL options select the defaults
of
.BR libmpq__archive_create (3).
The code must contain at least 32 bytes. The writer borrows the code during
creation, derives a private working key and clears it during cleanup.
.PP
The logical MPQ is staged in an owner-only file in the system temporary
directory. The stage supplies read-back for v4 RAW MD5 and permitted weak
signatures. Strong signing remains unsupported for MPQE creation. Weak signing
for v4 requires RAW chunks to be disabled. Oversized SINGLE members still
require full-unit buffering.
.PP
The required write callback is called only during consuming archive close.
It receives sequential ranges of encrypted transport. The read callback may be
NULL for all versions and is never invoked. The optional flush runs once after
successful writes and stage cleanup. The sink, context and callback pointers
remain borrowed through close, including failed close. A NULL context is valid.
Transfers must be exact, and callbacks must not re-enter the active writer.
See
.BR libmpq__archive_create_io (3)
for offset, buffer lifetime and synchronization rules.
.PP
The library never closes, frees, truncates, deletes or publishes caller storage.
Its own stage is closed before removal. A crash or cleanup failure can leave a
private plaintext stage behind. A failed close can leave partial or complete
transport in the sink. The caller controls disposal, publication and
persistence. MPQE encryption does not independently authenticate an archive.
.SH RETURN VALUE
Zero on success. Creation clears a provided output pointer before validation.
A missing output pointer or write callback returns
.BR LIBMPQ_ERROR_EXIST .
A missing or short code returns
.BR LIBMPQ_ERROR_DECRYPT .
Invalid options return
.BR LIBMPQ_ERROR_FORMAT .
Temporary storage and serialization failures return the corresponding libmpq
error. Close consumes the handle and preserves the first failure.
Negative callback errors propagate. A positive write status maps to
.B LIBMPQ_ERROR_WRITE
and a positive flush status maps to
.BR LIBMPQ_ERROR_CLOSE .
The writer stops issuing callbacks after a failure.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR libmpq (3),
.BR libmpq__archive_create_io (3),
.BR libmpq__archive_create_mpqe (3),
.BR libmpq__archive_open_mpqe_io (3),
.BR libmpq__archive_close (3),
.BR libmpq__archive_sign (3)
